            <ArticleTitle>To Err is Human: Can American Medicine Learn from Past Mistakes?</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.7812/TPP/16-181</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The history of medicine includes many errors. Some persisted for decades and caused great harm. Several are highlighted in this article, including the mythical thymic diseases: thymic asthma and status thymicolymphaticus. Some medical mistakes, such as the diet-heart hypothesis of Ancel Keys, continue to cause harm. To avoid future errors and their associated harm, I suggest a cultural shift encouraging professional humility and greater questioning of medical dogma. Medical education focused on teaching students this history may help with this cultural shift.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
